From: max994-dev <bmax994@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 02:34:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 13/13] run_one.py: run a single broker for a single customer
 on demand; Street falls back to Address; demyst postal code

run_one.py <user_id> <broker> [--address ... --city ... --state ... --zip ... --save]
drives the normal removal_dispatch path for one row, claims it so manage.py
cannot collide, uploads the screenshot to the customer's evidence and sets the
step like the main loop. Needed to produce one customer's oregonarrest.org
submission while they wait, instead of hours in the fair-share queue.

__removal.py: the PHP seeders never write data.street, so dataRow[Street] was
empty for every customer; it now falls back to the address.
demystcom.py: postal code was filled from Area Code, now from Zipcode.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
